comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T16:42:25.670Z","harness:codex","Implementation start: active in the shared runtime-capability-contracts bundle. Duplicate check covered all 2,136 tracker items and live GitHub reports; this item owns a distinct acceptance facet and will share exact-head verification with the related active items."
  "2026-07-27T18:19:06.330Z","harness:codex","Evidence: all dedicated MCP schemas now project from canonical SDK action/flag contracts through buildPmActionToolInputSchema; the conformance test rejects any non-transport schema key without a canonical backing property. Contract snapshot/check and the 38-test MCP focused suite pass warning-clean."
  "2026-07-27T20:33:06.688Z","harness:codex","Exact-head Greptile P1 remediation: verified that runtime custom fields named cwd, path, or options could overwrite canonical MCP schema keys and move transport arguments into the mutation options bag. Runtime projection now leaves every existing canonical property intact; normalization derives reserved names from TOOL_SCHEMA_BASE and the canonical action schema before moving custom inputs. A real temporary tracker registers all three colliding fields and verifies stable workspace routing plus nested custom values. The finding was up-voted, answered inline, and resolved. Verification: focused runtime suite, full typechecks, ESLint, zero duplicates, strict static/docstring quality, contract drift, and 379-file/6,428-test coverage at 100% statements (44,601/44,601), branches (31,721/31,721), functions (9,138/9,138), and lines (43,318/43,318)."
  "2026-07-27T20:51:43.947Z","harness:codex","Hosted-analysis follow-up: DeepScan reported NULL_POINTER at the new test's optional canonicalCreate access. Queried the exact public analysis API for defect 231228873, confirmed the warning, and replaced optional access with an explicit invariant guard before dereference. Focused runtime tests, complete TypeScript/package/example checks, ESLint, zero-duplication, strict static/docstring quality, SDK snapshots, and transport benchmarks pass. The prior authoritative full coverage remains 100/100/100/100 because this follow-up changes only the test invariant; final-head CI will rerun all four coverage shards."
  "2026-07-27T21:46:15.463Z","harness:codex","Final verification evidence: normalization now derives canonical reserved keys from the actual MCP tool definition, including tool-specific inputs such as allowMissingParent, while preserving nested custom values for colliding runtime fields. Linked handshake (33 tests), runtime capability (6 tests), and contracts snapshot checks pass. The isolated extension install regression test passed in 12 seconds; bounded-worker full coverage then passed 379 files and 6,428 tests at 100% statements (44,603/44,603), branches (31,721/31,721), functions (9,139/9,139), and lines (43,319/43,319). TypeScript, ESLint, zero-duplication, strict docstring/static quality, SDK snapshots, and the six-operation transport floor are green."
